  "prediction": "#507 phase 1: b_ref removes the XBOX load fast path (the per-TB preamble testing xbox_ram_fp.active/cb_count, and the per-load CBZ X26 + RAM/VRAM-window test) and returns X26/X27 to the register allocator. Loads take the softmmu TLB compare instead. The fast path read host_base+VA with no TLB lookup; where it was armed (activated after the first flip, and no NV2A surface watch live) and a page's VA differed from its RAM offset, it read the wrong page. Prediction: every capture in all 100 golden suites is bit-identical between arms, because either the path was never armed during a pgraph test or, when armed, the pages the test's loads touch map VA to the same RAM offset. A moved capture means the path was armed and read a different page than the TLB translation; a_ref's [mf0] lines in that run's logcat (act, cb, ln/vn/lo/vo) say which, and the move is then a correctness fix, not a regression.",
